SUMMARY:Maria Schneider Orchestra
LOCATION:Birdland Jazz Club\, Hell's Kitchen
DESCRIPTION:Maria Schneiders music has been hailed by critics as evocative\
 
, majestic\, magical\, heart-stoppingly gorgeous\, and beyond categorizatio
 
n. She and her 18-member orchestra have performed at concert halls around t
 
he world and have received 7 GRAMMYs\, many Jazz Journalist Awards\, and nu
 
merous DOWNBEAT and JAZZTIMES Readers and Critics Polls. Schneiders music b
 
lurs the lines between genres\, making her long list of commissioners quite
 
 varied\, stretching from jazz to classical\, and dance\, even collaboratin
 
g with David Bowie. She is among a small few to have received GRAMMYs in mu
 
ltiple genres\, having received the award in both jazz and classical\, as w
 
ell as for her work with David Bowie. Shes holds honorary doctorates from t
 
he University of Minnesota and Eastman School of Music. In 2019\, the Natio
 
nal Endowment for the Arts bestowed on Schneider the nations highest honor 
 
in jazz\, naming her an NEA Jazz Master. Musicians performing in her orches
 
tra throughout this week at Birdland are\, Reeds: Steve Wilson\, Dave Pietr
 
o\, Rich Perry\, Donny McCaslin\, John Ellis\, Scott Robinson Trumpets: Ton
 
y Kadleck\, Greg Gisbert\, Nadje Noordhuis\, Michael Dudley\, Mike Rodrigue
 
z Trombones: Keith OQuinn\, Ryan Keberle\, Marshall Gilkes\, George Flynn A
 
ccordion: Julien Labro Guitar: Jeff Miles Piano: Gary Versace Bass: Jay And
 
erson Drums: Johnathan Blake\, Rudy Royston For more information\, please v
 
isit: https://www.mariaschneider.com/ Tickets & info: https://www.ticketweb
 
.com/event/maria-schneider-orchestra-birdland-jazz-club-tickets/15005343
URL:https://www.ticketweb.com/event/maria-schneider-orchestra-birdland-jazz
 
-club-tickets/15005343
END:VEVENT
